.github/workflows/swiftc-corpus.yml

## YAML lint result

python3 -c "import yaml; yaml.safe_load(open('.github/workflows/swiftc-corpus.yml'))"
exit_code=0  (PASS — no YAML syntax errors)

## Summary

Three jobs created:
- compile: checkout + setup-swift@v2 (6.0) + make compile + upload out/*.so artifact (7-day retention)
- parity:  download artifact + setup-go@v6 + setup-swift@v2 + make extract + make oracle CORPUS=/tmp/corpus-regen.txt + drift check + go test TestThreeWayParity
- bench:   (optional) go test BenchmarkRemangle — graceful skip if benchmark not yet present

## Security notes

- github.event.pull_request.title passed via env var PR_TITLE (not interpolated directly into run: shell)
- No other untrusted inputs used in shell commands

## Issues found

None. YAML lint clean, paths verified against Makefile and corpus_swiftc_test.go.

## Corpus drift check logic

make oracle is run with CORPUS=/tmp/corpus-regen.txt so the committed corpus.txt
is not overwritten. The drift check diffs corpus.txt (committed) vs /tmp/corpus-regen.txt
(freshly generated). Fails unless PR title contains [corpus-bump].
